body:
> @HEX-23 Would you be willing to make a separate PR to add AMBIENT_LIGHT to the light() and fragment() functions? That would be useful to expose I think, I definitely have a few things it would be nice for

@coobenguy I skimmed through the code, and it seems that ambient light is resolved only _after_ fragment(), as it depends on things like user-specified normal and other surface properties (which are _output_ of fragment()).

I suggest that you open an issue in the [godot-proposals repo](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues) about this (adding it to fragment() is not quite possible imo, but it might be made accessible in light(), I guess. If you can give some (preferably popular) example use cases of the feature in that issue, then there is a higher chance that it would be implemented and merged).
